WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.268
You're about to leave for a weekend
away. You remember saving where

00:00:04.268 --> 00:00:08.535
you put the spare keys, but not where.
Ask Pocket Memory: Where

00:00:08.535 --> 00:00:12.803
did I keep the spare keys? Llama finds
the saved note: the

00:00:12.803 --> 00:00:17.071
blue pouch in the front pocket of your
grey backpack. The source

00:00:17.071 --> 00:00:20.983
stays visible, so you can check it.
Useful details, without searching

00:00:20.983 --> 00:00:22.050
through every note.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:28.185
Now a client changes a video brief.
Friday becomes Monday. English captions

00:00:28.185 --> 00:00:33.320
become Hindi. Save the correction and
ask about the updated brief. Here,

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.456
the model's answer could not be
verified, so Pocket Memory shows the

00:00:38.456 --> 00:00:42.735
original updated note. Monday evening.
Hindi captions. The earlier wording

00:00:42.735 --> 00:00:47.870
remains in history. You can check what
changed before doing the work,

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.010
without trusting an unsupported answer.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.540
Before your trip, you want to use Google
Maps offline. Turn on

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.070
Search the web and ask how to download
an area on Android.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:04.600
Pocket Memory uses one MCP search, then
Llama reads the results on

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.130
your phone and returns source links.
Your private key-location note is not

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.282
attached. Check the official source,
then follow the steps when you're

00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:13.660
ready.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:19.675
Need the client's updated brief while
working in your browser? Open the

00:01:19.675 --> 00:01:24.272
WebMCP companion from Android Settings.
A permitted browser agent can search

00:01:24.272 --> 00:01:29.286
Cedar Studio and retrieve the current
saved note. The app still runs

00:01:29.286 --> 00:01:34.301
on your phone. Browser access expires,
and requests are limited. Your chosen

00:01:34.301 --> 00:01:38.480
browser agent may process returned
content under its own policy.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.762
Download Llama inside Models, then tap
Use this model. After setup,

00:01:44.762 --> 00:01:49.564
saved-memory answers work offline. These
are real Llama results with

00:01:49.564 --> 00:01:54.846
fictional examples, edited from actual
app captures. Pocket Memory's core is

00:01:54.846 --> 00:02:00.128
the existing foundation. This edition
adds the Llama setup, guarded MCP

00:02:00.128 --> 00:02:04.450
search and WebMCP companion. Physical-
phone testing is still pending.
